  "answer": "This has been reported before. Keycap emoji such as 1️⃣ are several codepoints joined together: the digit, U+FE0F and U+20E3. Windows Terminal doesn't handle that sequence well, so the digit and the box get drawn misaligned. The unrelated 🔟 has its own single codepoint, which is why it renders fine. In terminal#9708 a maintainer ([user]) said the fix is to add custom keycap detection to the font fallback (MapCharacters) logic. The ticket doesn't record a fix or a configuration workaround. Please add your version (1.24) and screenshots to that ticket, and follow it for updates. Until it's fixed, avoid keycap emoji in file and directory names, or use a different character such as 🔟 or plain digits."
